    "text": {
     "en": "Choose a sensible unit: centimetres for a pencil, metres for a room, kilometres for a road.\nEstimate first by guessing a length using something you know, like the width of your hand or the height of the door.\nThen measure to check. Your estimates get better with practice.\nWhich tools can measure height besides a tape? A measuring rod or a scale on the wall."
